WEBVTT

00:12.990 --> 00:15.660
TOMB RAIDER KING

01:31.110 --> 01:32.810
Here's our first bidder.

01:32.810 --> 01:33.740
You know who he is?

01:33.740 --> 01:35.070
EPISODE 5: THE KING OF THE HERB OF ETERNAL LIFE
Who's that guy?

01:35.070 --> 01:37.850
EPISODE 5: THE KING OF THE HERB OF ETERNAL LIFE
Another bidder just raised their hand.

01:38.750 --> 01:42.750
I knew it.
So Kwon noticed it too?

01:43.830 --> 01:48.050
The legendary emperor
who wielded power in Ancient Dahlia.

01:49.350 --> 01:53.840
This is indeed the Herb of Eternal Life
that he was desperately searching for

01:53.840 --> 01:55.410
in his quest for eternal life.

01:56.850 --> 02:00.890
Before returning to the past,
my body, wrecked by relics,

02:00.890 --> 02:04.350
would've turned to dust were it not
for the Herb of Eternal Life.

02:05.240 --> 02:08.190
I took on every dirty job imaginable

02:08.610 --> 02:11.290
just to get my hands on that fruit
that Kwon possessed.

02:14.050 --> 02:16.400
It was, so to speak, my lifeline.

02:18.080 --> 02:21.700
Old Kwon... Did he get the herb here?

02:22.350 --> 02:26.400
If he takes that from me, I'll end up
repeating the same future as before.

02:26.400 --> 02:27.710
I must obtain it!

02:27.710 --> 02:30.200
That's a great reaction.

02:30.200 --> 02:33.590
I suppose so, for this almond here...

02:34.030 --> 02:37.600
Apparently it's incredibly effective
for boosting sexual stamina.

02:40.010 --> 02:42.220
You clueless idiots!

02:42.220 --> 02:44.070
What on earth makes that a sex drug?!

02:47.130 --> 02:51.610
Well then, in response to your enthusiasm,
we'll start at two hundred thousand dollars.

02:52.030 --> 02:53.300
Five hundred thousand!

02:53.300 --> 02:54.790
Five hundred five thousand!

02:54.790 --> 02:55.930
Five hundred thousand?

02:56.520 --> 02:59.120
What the hell, that isn't even a sex drug!

02:59.120 --> 03:00.710
Ten million.

03:01.850 --> 03:03.120
Chairman?!

03:06.640 --> 03:09.630
The hell? Ten million dollars?

03:09.630 --> 03:11.120
Fifteen million.

03:11.690 --> 03:13.090
Twenty million.

03:13.090 --> 03:14.380
Twenty two!

03:14.760 --> 03:16.380
Forty million.

03:16.380 --> 03:17.710
Forty five million!

03:17.710 --> 03:19.010
Fifty million!

03:19.010 --> 03:20.960
Will that even work?

03:20.960 --> 03:22.010
Who knows?

03:22.010 --> 03:25.230
You're kidding me.
Fifty million?

03:25.230 --> 03:27.020
I didn't expect that.

03:27.410 --> 03:29.050
One hundred million dollars.

03:29.050 --> 03:30.020
Chairman!

03:31.920 --> 03:33.150
Miss Irene.

03:35.070 --> 03:36.950
Well then...

03:36.950 --> 03:38.570
One hundred fifty million.

03:39.070 --> 03:40.950
One hundred fifty million?

03:45.280 --> 03:47.460
One hundred fifty million!

03:47.460 --> 03:49.580
Who's that?

03:49.960 --> 03:52.590
Time for her to tag me out here.

03:53.590 --> 03:55.340
One hundred sixty million!

03:55.990 --> 03:57.270
Two hundred million!

03:59.010 --> 04:01.800
How dare she suddenly barge in
and cause a commotion!

04:01.800 --> 04:05.490
Chairman, I'm sorry, but it seems
we should probably call it quits.

04:05.490 --> 04:09.060
That's Irene Holton, the youngest
daughter of the Holton family!

04:09.060 --> 04:10.530
So what?

04:10.530 --> 04:12.110
Two hundred twenty million!

04:12.110 --> 04:13.110
Chairman!

04:13.560 --> 04:15.310
Please calm down!

04:15.310 --> 04:18.350
We don't have deeper pockets
than the Holton family!

04:18.350 --> 04:19.870
Three hundred million.

04:21.970 --> 04:23.490
Three hundred...

04:24.040 --> 04:25.790
Get off me!

04:25.790 --> 04:28.000
You can't! Please hold it in!

04:28.000 --> 04:30.570
Calm down, Sir!

04:30.570 --> 04:32.500
I beg you!

04:33.360 --> 04:35.470
We have a winner.

04:39.290 --> 04:40.510
Please wait a moment.

04:41.170 --> 04:42.830
We'll prepare it for you now.

04:42.830 --> 04:44.210
All right.

04:46.170 --> 04:47.760
You saved my bacon.

04:47.760 --> 04:50.770
But that must have been a painful
expense because of me, right?

04:51.530 --> 04:55.400
Not at all, if you're going
to solve my problem.

04:55.960 --> 04:59.830
I wonder if there's a way
to share some good luck.

04:59.830 --> 05:01.410
Like a talisman...

05:01.830 --> 05:05.010
No, I'm not giving you anything.

05:05.010 --> 05:07.410
I'm just taking what you have.

05:08.390 --> 05:12.920
For example, there must be this
strange thing that follows you around.

05:13.830 --> 05:15.160
Please give me that.

05:15.160 --> 05:17.420
If you do that,
your misfortune will disappear.

05:19.030 --> 05:22.230
It would be enough just to get rid
of the bankruptcy relic,

05:22.230 --> 05:26.100
but since I get to keep it too,
it's like killing two birds with one stone.

05:27.010 --> 05:29.960
Something that follows me around?

05:29.960 --> 05:32.100
I don't have anything
that comes to mind.

05:33.470 --> 05:36.280
That's weird...
She doesn't have such a thing?

05:38.170 --> 05:42.780
If that's the case, did a tattoo
suddenly appear on your body?

05:44.760 --> 05:46.070
Bingo.

05:46.070 --> 05:50.140
Tattoos that appear on the body are
a characteristic of possession relics.

05:50.140 --> 05:55.210
The tattoo on Sasaki Yuka's arm is proof that she
has entered into a contract with the Future Guide

05:55.210 --> 05:57.130
and has become its owner.

05:58.000 --> 06:01.320
Unlike consumable relics,
which anyone can use,

06:01.320 --> 06:06.420
possession-type relics can only
be used by their owners.

06:09.680 --> 06:12.310
I'll show you the picture.

06:13.180 --> 06:14.300
Here it is.

06:18.320 --> 06:20.160
Hang on...

06:20.160 --> 06:22.320
This is a parasitic relic.

06:23.300 --> 06:28.100
A very rare type of relic that
parasitises its host's body.

06:28.100 --> 06:31.830
Unlike the possession-type ones,
you can't simply steal its power.

06:32.510 --> 06:35.830
I thought it would be an easy fix,
but it seems I was wrong.

06:36.430 --> 06:38.710
Let's take our time to find a solution.

06:41.280 --> 06:42.930
This is my number.

06:42.930 --> 06:45.970
I won't run away or anything.
Don't worry.

06:47.520 --> 06:49.560
Okay, thank you.

06:50.000 --> 06:53.420
If I can't take her power away,
I'll just keep her by my side.

06:53.420 --> 06:55.010
Thank you for your patience.

06:56.210 --> 06:59.570
Here are the almond sapling
and other items.

07:00.050 --> 07:04.900
You may take home any items other than
almond sapling after you have paid.

07:05.380 --> 07:09.910
Since there are quite a few items,
would you like us to carry them for you?

07:10.420 --> 07:14.100
No, thank you.
I'll figure something out.

07:20.500 --> 07:22.920
He's not answering... How come?

07:23.620 --> 07:25.460
Don't tell me those guys...

07:27.570 --> 07:28.930
Boss!

07:28.930 --> 07:31.870
Now that we've made it this far,
there's no way he can follow us!

07:31.870 --> 07:34.460
That's right, let's take a little break!

07:34.460 --> 07:36.830
Wanna do that?

07:40.850 --> 07:43.150
- We're rich!
- Rich!

07:43.150 --> 07:44.540
Rich!

07:44.540 --> 07:47.330
Just thinking about how we'll be
able to play around forever

07:47.330 --> 07:50.390
from now on makes my heart race!

08:01.540 --> 08:04.300
You've got balls trying to
run away with my money.

08:05.540 --> 08:07.800
Joo-Heon?! How did you find us?!

08:09.260 --> 08:13.570
How? The Silver Axe
just told me straight away.

08:13.570 --> 08:16.390
Hey, Joo-Heon...

08:16.390 --> 08:17.390
Shut up!

08:18.350 --> 08:20.150
I gotta punish you now.

08:23.810 --> 08:27.150
Is that a pumice stone for exfoliating?

08:27.150 --> 08:29.660
Huh? It's shining...

08:36.130 --> 08:39.760
The code of laws created by
King Hammurabi of ancient Babylonia.

08:39.760 --> 08:44.049
It's the one famous for the phrase
"an eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth".

08:44.049 --> 08:48.170
A counter-type relic that simply returns
the attack the opponent initiated.

08:48.750 --> 08:51.650
I just won this at the auction today.

08:52.740 --> 08:56.680
I brought it up first, but this is
a good opportunity to give it a try.

08:58.130 --> 09:02.690
An eye for an eye, a tooth for a tooth,
and a betrayal for a betrayal.

09:05.010 --> 09:06.150
What?!

09:13.980 --> 09:17.640
It is essentially a power that allows you
to counter an enemy's attack.

09:18.580 --> 09:24.170
But the Code is something that can even
restrict the target's future actions.

09:24.170 --> 09:25.230
CODE OF HAMMURABI

09:25.230 --> 09:27.670
THE RELIC IS WATCHING OVER THE TARGETS
That's what the law is all about.

09:29.820 --> 09:32.720
What the? What was that?

09:32.720 --> 09:34.560
I wonder...

09:34.560 --> 09:37.870
Nothing should happen as long
as you don't betray me.

09:37.870 --> 09:42.440
But if you betray me,
you'll be torn to pieces.

09:44.720 --> 09:46.140
Okay, we get it!

09:46.140 --> 09:47.880
We won't do that again!

09:50.460 --> 09:51.970
Let's begin now.

09:51.970 --> 09:52.740
Hey!

09:52.740 --> 09:54.720
- It's embarrassing if you put me out of the pot!
- Your job is to harvest

09:54.720 --> 09:56.490
- What are you doing?!
- the fruit from this thing.

09:56.490 --> 09:59.900
- Put me back again!
- Fruit, you say?

10:00.770 --> 10:03.500
Put me back to the pot!

10:03.500 --> 10:06.670
- You bunch of goofballs!
- Repot it right away.

10:06.670 --> 10:08.920
It's been screaming at my ears nonstop.

10:08.920 --> 10:10.450
I'll curse you!

10:10.450 --> 10:13.170
- You won't get away with this!
- For now...

10:14.430 --> 10:15.700
Hey, don't touch me!

10:15.700 --> 10:18.430
Okay, calm down.

10:18.430 --> 10:19.870
It's actually quite pleasing.

10:19.870 --> 10:21.930
Yeah?

10:23.460 --> 10:25.120
Yeah!

10:25.660 --> 10:27.970
The tip of that branch.
It might be a little stiff.

10:27.970 --> 10:30.650
I didn't expect that.
He's got high Affinity.

10:31.650 --> 10:32.430
Go away!

10:32.430 --> 10:33.890
- Last night, I tried to contract it
- Get off me!

10:33.890 --> 10:35.410
- to my possession,
- Get off me!

10:35.410 --> 10:37.310
- but it fell through because
- The nerve of a human!

10:37.310 --> 10:38.910
- this guy went on a rampage.
- The nerve of a human!

10:40.860 --> 10:43.910
- That hurts!
- Hey, put it in more gently!

10:43.910 --> 10:45.460
It'll curse us!

10:45.460 --> 10:48.930
So the herb prefers humans
with high Affinity?

10:48.930 --> 10:50.920
I guess they're the right men for the job.

10:55.430 --> 10:58.430
INCOMING CALL
This number looks familiar.

10:58.910 --> 11:02.980
The fact that they're reaching out is proof
that they've started trying to figure me out.

11:03.950 --> 11:05.660
Hello?

11:06.380 --> 11:08.480
Seo Joo-Heon?

11:08.480 --> 11:11.330
I'm Kwon Tae-Joon from TKBM.

11:11.860 --> 11:15.110
Hello, Mister Kwon.
What do you need?

11:15.620 --> 11:17.570
Let me get straight to the point.

11:17.570 --> 11:22.050
I hear you have the tree that
Irene Holton won at auction?

11:22.580 --> 11:25.420
I'd like to talk to you about that...

11:25.420 --> 11:28.340
I don't have anything
to discuss about that.

11:29.710 --> 11:31.130
Insolent brat!

11:32.530 --> 11:35.930
Chairman, I'll bring that tree over.

11:35.930 --> 11:37.930
You?

11:38.950 --> 11:42.000
Yes, if it's okay to use
the company's relic,

11:42.000 --> 11:43.930
I’ll take care of everything.

11:44.410 --> 11:48.000
He's just an ordinary person,
so it's not that hard.

11:48.000 --> 11:52.320
I need to resolve this situation
and score some brownie points.

12:04.990 --> 12:07.830
It's been a few days after
the Silver Axe started reacting

12:08.460 --> 12:11.340
It seems the investigation
on me has already begun.

12:12.060 --> 12:14.580
I didn't think it would take this long.

12:14.580 --> 12:17.170
I was just starting
to get tired of waiting.

12:17.680 --> 12:19.110
Excuse me.

12:19.110 --> 12:20.110
Finally.

12:20.110 --> 12:22.430
Mister Seo Joo-Heon?

12:22.430 --> 12:25.100
Yoon Si-Woo.
He's on his own?

12:26.400 --> 12:28.940
Looks like they're looking down on me.

12:31.710 --> 12:34.050
Um, Mister Seo?

12:34.650 --> 12:37.310
Nice. He really has a relic.

12:41.120 --> 12:42.990
Hey! Can't you hear me?!

12:42.990 --> 12:45.830
It's common courtesy to answer
when someone talks to you!

12:48.560 --> 12:51.000
Oh, my apologies.

12:51.460 --> 12:53.570
You just started yelling out of the blue.

12:53.570 --> 12:55.500
It really startled me.

12:56.530 --> 12:57.810
You prick...

12:59.540 --> 13:01.570
Don't act dumb.

13:01.570 --> 13:04.140
We met at the Midas auction, didn't we?!

13:04.140 --> 13:05.820
We did?

13:05.820 --> 13:09.490
Oh, I remember!
The chairman's goldfish poop!

13:10.350 --> 13:14.630
Poop?! What the hell?!

13:14.630 --> 13:15.860
WHEN THE OPPONENT LOSES COMPOSURE,

13:15.860 --> 13:18.570
THEIR DOMINANCE WILL WEAKEN TEMPORARILY
So this is his weakness.

13:20.020 --> 13:21.600
Yoon Si-Woo.

13:21.600 --> 13:26.540
He tries his hardest to put on a brave face,
but he's a bundle of insecurities.

13:26.540 --> 13:31.460
If you pushed that button, he couldn't control
his anger and ended up blowing himself up.

13:32.330 --> 13:35.260
Since the power of Dominance
is affected by one's mental state,

13:35.260 --> 13:40.420
this guy having lost his rationality,
was no longer able to use high-level relics.

13:40.900 --> 13:44.910
Right, I did get a call from the chairman.

13:45.950 --> 13:49.100
Does he really need that almond?

13:49.100 --> 13:51.340
Talk about being too desperate.

13:53.170 --> 13:55.690
What?!
You bastard!

14:05.760 --> 14:07.950
How do I do this, again?

14:11.970 --> 14:13.870
My nose...

14:14.560 --> 14:18.590
Someone with waning Dominance like you
could never use a relic.

14:19.180 --> 14:22.590
You knew about the relics?!

14:22.590 --> 14:26.500
Obviously. I'll take good care of this.

14:26.500 --> 14:29.350
You won't get away...

14:32.510 --> 14:34.050
You're a possession-type, huh?

14:34.050 --> 14:36.830
- Your new owner is me now.
- Don't...

14:39.180 --> 14:41.280
Who might you be?

14:41.280 --> 14:44.720
Oh? That is quite strong Dominance you have.

14:44.720 --> 14:47.700
Feel free to use me.

14:49.360 --> 14:51.750
Stop! Don't do that!

14:55.360 --> 15:00.210
Voodoo Priest's Zombie Powder.
An A Rank possession-type relic.

15:00.210 --> 15:03.210
Voodoo, which originated
among slaves in Africa,

15:03.210 --> 15:07.010
holds the belief that those who commit sins
will be punished by becoming zombies.

15:08.380 --> 15:10.860
If you touch or inhale this powder,

15:10.860 --> 15:13.870
you will temporarily lose your sanity
and turn into a zombie.

15:15.630 --> 15:18.020
To think he got outplayed
by his own relic...

15:18.770 --> 15:22.270
This should keep Kwon
from tracking me for a while.

15:27.390 --> 15:29.250
Is he one of yours?

15:41.360 --> 15:43.380
What is that idiot doing?!

15:43.380 --> 15:46.840
Apparently, he was pretending
to be a zombie on the street.

15:47.220 --> 15:49.850
It seems they'll be conducting
drug tests on him as well...

15:50.300 --> 15:54.350
Forget about Yoon!
Go get back the relic that guy took!

15:54.350 --> 15:59.100
About that, he didn't have it with him
when they found him...

15:59.100 --> 16:00.740
What?

16:03.010 --> 16:04.830
Get me Attorney Lee Jin-Ah!

16:04.830 --> 16:06.110
Sir!

16:06.670 --> 16:10.620
If it's come to this, we have no choice
but to change our strategy.

16:13.660 --> 16:18.120
My back hurts! Oww...

16:18.120 --> 16:20.370
Hey, Jeo-Hoon...

16:20.370 --> 16:21.380
Call me Boss.

16:21.380 --> 16:26.510
Do we have to carry all this luggage?

16:26.510 --> 16:28.990
Take everything with us.

16:28.990 --> 16:30.890
It'll be our war chest.

16:32.800 --> 16:34.930
They don't look that expensive...

16:35.580 --> 16:38.060
I was able to get so many relics.

16:38.700 --> 16:41.390
You could say this is a stroke of luck, too.

16:41.920 --> 16:47.310
For now, I've got the Egyptian Funeral Knife,
the Gold and Silver Axe,

16:47.310 --> 16:49.820
the Rope, and the Muramasa.

16:49.820 --> 16:52.880
Also, all the items I won at auction,
the Code of Hammurabi,

16:52.880 --> 16:56.340
Shakespeare's Pen,
Marie Antoinette's necklace,

16:56.340 --> 16:59.220
and the Emperor's Herb of Eternal Life.

16:59.760 --> 17:02.610
Then, the Zombie Powder
I took from Yoon,

17:02.610 --> 17:06.859
wealth-type Foxtail Millet,
and Homeros' Glasses.

17:06.859 --> 17:09.410
This should be more than enough
as start-up capital.

17:09.410 --> 17:11.619
I should be able to gather more relics.

17:11.619 --> 17:12.990
Mister Seo.

17:12.990 --> 17:13.970
Huh?

17:16.400 --> 17:19.430
I'm Lee Jin-Ah, an attorney for TKBM.

17:19.940 --> 17:21.940
Here she comes.

17:25.940 --> 17:28.940
There's no need to be on your guard.

17:28.940 --> 17:33.260
Chairman Kwon holds your abilities
in high regard.

17:34.690 --> 17:38.820
I've come to propose a contract
with the TKBM Excavation Team.

17:39.660 --> 17:42.210
The contract amount is $100 million.

17:42.210 --> 17:44.960
Of course, we'll also pay you
a separate monthly salary.

17:44.960 --> 17:47.960
We won't interfere with your personal life.

17:48.660 --> 17:51.170
You'll only be listed under TKBM...

17:51.760 --> 17:54.220
I was wondering what this was all about,

17:54.220 --> 17:57.330
but it turns out you just want me
to sign a slave contract.

17:57.330 --> 18:00.310
Mister Seo, you better watch your mouth.

18:00.930 --> 18:03.680
What do you plan to do
if the chairman takes action

18:03.680 --> 18:06.860
against you for taking Mister Yoon's stuff?

18:06.860 --> 18:10.800
He can make places like that gallery
disappear without a trace,

18:10.800 --> 18:14.870
and your subordinates might lose
their lives to a mysterious illness.

18:14.870 --> 18:17.620
And you're no exception.

18:19.520 --> 18:22.620
So you're saying if I don't want to die,
I have to serve you guys?

18:23.410 --> 18:28.130
Miss Lawyer, you'd better choose
carefully who to pick a fight with.

18:30.130 --> 18:33.880
Right now, it's you who's going
to disappear without a trace.

18:33.880 --> 18:35.920
Zombie Powder?

18:35.920 --> 18:37.950
There's no point in putting on a brave face.

18:37.950 --> 18:41.220
You can't possibly use the relic
in a place this crowded.

18:41.220 --> 18:43.280
Really?

18:43.280 --> 18:45.230
Try me.

18:45.760 --> 18:46.860
You're crazy!

18:50.020 --> 18:51.410
Water Cannon!

18:59.160 --> 19:01.450
An eye for an eye,
a tooth for a tooth.

19:02.000 --> 19:05.540
A Water Cannon for a Water Cannon!

19:13.880 --> 19:15.820
- That's amusing!
- Something's going on there!

19:15.820 --> 19:17.520
That's strange.

19:17.520 --> 19:18.890
What is it?

19:22.830 --> 19:25.390
The audience has started to gather, so...

19:27.230 --> 19:29.330
Let's finish this.

19:31.820 --> 19:33.900
Nooooo!!

19:34.660 --> 19:36.910
Requesting backup,
I repeat, requesting backup.

19:36.910 --> 19:40.410
An explosion was heard coming from
the café. Could be a terrorist.

19:40.410 --> 19:42.140
- Requesting backup at once.
- Hurry!

19:42.140 --> 19:45.710
A naked woman is attacking
passersby near the café!

19:46.130 --> 19:46.980
Over here!

19:46.980 --> 19:48.040
Got it!

19:52.700 --> 19:53.620
PARIS MONMARTRE PAINTER'S INK

19:53.620 --> 19:55.050
(RANK B RARE-TIER CONSUMABLE RELIC)
USES LEFT: 50/100

19:55.050 --> 19:58.880
All right.
I came across something unexpected.

19:58.880 --> 20:02.430
Human, face where my voice is.

20:02.430 --> 20:04.530
That place is at risk.

20:04.530 --> 20:06.060
Crow?

20:07.570 --> 20:11.580
What do you mean crow? You keep
muttering at yourself looking at the sky.

20:12.740 --> 20:14.070
Something wrong?

20:14.770 --> 20:17.070
Looks like they can't hear the Crow.

20:17.470 --> 20:19.820
Hurry up and come over here.

20:19.820 --> 20:22.530
How dare you, a mere relic,
try to boss me around!

20:22.530 --> 20:25.740
Sending me back in time
without any explanation...

20:25.740 --> 20:29.660
And you just keep giving orders
without answering any of my questions!

20:29.660 --> 20:31.520
You will regret it.

20:32.290 --> 20:34.990
You think I'll believe
what a relic's saying?!

20:39.010 --> 20:41.510
You seem to be having fun over there.

20:47.660 --> 20:49.270
Mister Seo Joo-Heon.

20:49.680 --> 20:51.270
Kwon Tae-Joon...

20:57.170 --> 21:01.700
Hey, isn't it the real Kwon?
What's going on here? Are we okay?

21:01.700 --> 21:04.950
I am Kwon Tae-Joon from TKBM.

21:04.950 --> 21:09.020
Oh, yes, hello...

21:09.020 --> 21:10.940
Pipe down.

21:14.370 --> 21:15.960
Boss, what's wrong?!

21:15.960 --> 21:18.290
- It hurts!
- Are you okay?!

21:22.960 --> 21:24.470
Damn it!

23:03.700 --> 23:05.860
You even obtained the Herb of Eternal Life.

23:05.860 --> 23:09.100
I have enough power to handle that, after all.

23:09.100 --> 23:12.000
Do you think your power alone will suffice?

23:12.000 --> 23:15.370
You will regret turning down my proposal.

23:15.370 --> 23:17.120
Be my guest.

23:17.120 --> 23:20.260
Still, to think the final boss
would show up this quick...

23:20.260 --> 23:23.460
Seems like TKBM doesn't have that
many promising human resources.

23:23.460 --> 23:26.350
The chairman will turn all the tables.

23:26.350 --> 23:29.010
Let's see how long you can keep
that smug talk.

23:29.010 --> 23:33.710
Oops, there goes the time
to deal with you now.

23:33.710 --> 23:36.100
Next time: The Great Entombment.

23:36.100 --> 23:38.880
EPISODE 6: THE GREAT ENTOMBMENT
The whole world might just change.

23:38.880 --> 23:42.180
EPISODE 6: THE GREAT ENTOMBMENT
